findings.fix:
In keepInBand (render-b.js:846) replace the unconditional re-centre `var delta = Math.round(top - Math.max(16, (free - height) / 2));` with a minimum correction that keeps a 24px margin, re-centring only when the row genuinely cannot fit the band:

  var pad = 24;
  var delta = height + pad * 2 > free
    ? Math.round(top - Math.max(16, (free - height) / 2))
    : (top < pad ? Math.round(top - pad) : Math.round(top + height - (free - pad)));

This turns the 1440 first press into a 26px correction and the 1280 one into 86px, leaves the fixed/docked sheet path at 390 and 768 behaving exactly as the two standing band assertions require (the row still lands inside the band, now with 24px of air rather than flush), and keeps the origin on screen. Ship it red-green with a new desk assertion, written to fail first: at 1152, 1279, 1280 and 1440 on owner-editing, press '+7' eight times and assert after every press that (a) .b-origin's box still intersects .b-plan's box, and (b) the change in pane.scrollTop is never greater than the row's own travel, 7 x Number(.b-measure[data-px]).
